  "question": {
    "text": "The differential equation representing the family of curves $y^2=2 c(x+\\sqrt{c})$, where $c$ $>0$, is a parameter, is of order and degree as follows:",
    "image": null
  },
  "options": [
    {
      "id": "85oMN",
      "text": "\norder 1 , degree 2\n",
      "image": null,
      "isCorrect": false
    },
    {
      "id": "s2ku8",
      "text": "\norder 1, degree 1\n",
      "image": null,
      "isCorrect": false
    },
    {
      "id": "lXsGG",
      "text": "\norder 1, degree 3\n",
      "image": null,
      "isCorrect": true
    },
    {
      "id": "UeU1P",
      "text": "\norder 2, degree 2",
      "image": null,
      "isCorrect": false
    }
  ],
  "correctValue": null,
  "solution": {
    "text": "$$\n\\begin{aligned}\n& y^2=2 c(x+\\sqrt{c} ) .....(i)\\\\\n& 2 y y^{\\prime}=2 c \\cdot 1 \\text { or } y y^{\\prime}=c ....(ii)\\\\\n& \\Rightarrow y^2=2 y y^{\\prime}\\left(x+\\sqrt{y y^{\\prime}}\\right)\n\\end{aligned}\n$$\n[on putting value of c from (ii) in (i)]\nOn simplifying, we get\n$$\n\\left(y-2 x y^{\\prime}\\right)^2=4 y y^{\\prime 3} .....(iii)\n$$\nHence equation (iii) is of order 1 and degree 3.",
    "image": null
  },
